#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:9
msgid "Transporting GPU buffers with ``rosidl::Buffer`` - tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:12
msgid ""
"High-bandwidth perception and tensor workloads can benefit from keeping "
"large payloads in GPU memory. This tutorial builds and runs a CUDA-backed "
"``rosidl::Buffer`` demo that compares zero-copy GPU transport with CPU "
"serialization. After following it, you will understand how to run the demo "
"and interpret its throughput results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:22
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:25
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:27
msgid ""
":doc:`rosidl::Buffer backends <About-Buffer-Backends>` let ROS 2 messages "
"carry large payloads (images, tensors, ...) in vendor-specific memory "
"domains such as GPU memory, with the descriptor round-trip handled "
"transparently by the RMW."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:32
msgid ""
"This demo exercises the full pipeline using the community-maintained CUDA "
"backend and the ``torch_conversions`` helper library. It publishes "
"``tensor_msgs/msg/ExperimentalTensor`` frames between two processes either "
"over a zero-copy CUDA path or over the traditional CPU-serialised path, and "
"compares throughput at several resolutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:38
msgid ""
"The underlying demo is maintained in `ros2/rosidl_buffer_backends_tutorials "
"<https://github.com/ros2/rosidl_buffer_backends_tutorials>`__; the package "
"name is ``robot_arm_demo``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:44
msgid "What the demo does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:46
msgid ""
"``robot_arm_demo`` renders an SDF-based pencil-sketch robot arm animation "
"entirely on the GPU via LibTorch tensor operations, publishes BGRA frames as "
"``tensor_msgs/msg/ExperimentalTensor``, and displays them in an SDL2/OpenGL "
"window with CUDA-GL interop. Two processes are involved:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:52
msgid ""
"``renderer_node`` -- renders BGRA frames on the GPU using LibTorch "
"operations, copies them into an ``ExperimentalTensor`` message with "
"``torch_conversions``, and publishes that message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:55
msgid ""
"``display_node`` -- subscribes to the tensor topic, wraps the received "
"message as an ``at::Tensor`` with ``torch_conversions``, displays frames, "
"and reports FPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:59
msgid "Two transport modes are compared:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:61
msgid ""
"**CUDA** -- the ``ExperimentalTensor.data`` field is backed by the ``cuda`` "
"buffer backend. The bytes never leave GPU memory: the descriptor on the wire "
"carries a small reference that lets the subscriber re-attach to the "
"publisher-owned CUDA allocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:64
msgid ""
"**CPU** -- the frame is rendered on the GPU, copied back to host memory with "
"``cudaMemcpy``, and then serialised through the RMW as a regular "
"``uint8[]``. The default CPU buffer backend is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:69
msgid ""
"Both modes render on the GPU; the only difference is the transport path, "
"making this a clean comparison of zero-copy CUDA IPC versus traditional CPU-"
"serialised image transport."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:74
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:76
msgid ""
"This demo is not part of the ROS 2 binary distribution; it lives in its own "
"repository and has GPU-specific dependencies. You need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:80
msgid "A CUDA-capable GPU and the CUDA Toolkit (>= 11.8)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:81
msgid "SDL2, GLEW, OpenGL, X11 development packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:82
msgid ""
"A ROS 2 Lyrical Luth or later source workspace. See the :doc:`Installation "
"instructions <../../../../Get-Started/Installation>` for the canonical "
"source-build flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:85
msgid "``rmw_fastrtps_cpp`` for the non-CPU buffer path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:87
msgid ""
"The demo's ``libtorch_vendor`` package will download and install a pre-built "
"LibTorch distribution automatically at build time if one is not already "
"visible on the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:92
msgid "Building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:94
msgid "Clone both repositories into your ROS 2 workspace's ``src/`` directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:96
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws/src\n"
"$ git clone https://github.com/ros2/rosidl_buffer_backends.git\n"
"$ git clone https://github.com/ros2/rosidl_buffer_backends_tutorials.git"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:102
msgid "Install the system dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:104
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws\n"
"$ rosdep install --from-paths src --ignore-src -y \\\n"
"    --skip-keys \"fastcdr rti-connext-dds-7.7.0 urdfdom_headers qt6-svg-dev\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:110
msgid ""
"Build ``torch_conversions`` and its CUDA transport dependency first, source "
"the workspace, then build the demo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:113
msgid ""
"$ colcon build --symlink-install --packages-up-to cuda_buffer_backend\n"
"$ source install/setup.sh\n"
"$ colcon build --symlink-install --packages-up-to robot_arm_demo\n"
"$ source install/setup.sh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:120
msgid ""
"The intermediate ``source install/setup.sh`` is required so that "
"``torch_conversions`` can discover ``cuda_buffer`` at CMake configure time "
"and compile its CUDA path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:125
msgid "Running"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:127
msgid ""
"The demo ships three launch files. Run them with "
"``RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_fastrtps_cpp`` when exercising the CUDA path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:132
msgid "CUDA zero-copy (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:134
msgid ""
"$ export RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_fastrtps_cpp\n"
"$ ros2 launch robot_arm_demo robot_arm_demo.launch.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:139
msgid ""
"The renderer and display processes negotiate the ``cuda`` backend for the "
"tensor message's data field; the payload never leaves GPU memory between the "
"two processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:144
msgid "CPU transport"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:146
msgid "$ ros2 launch robot_arm_demo robot_arm_demo.launch.py use_cuda:=false"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:150
msgid ""
"The subscription is not opted into any non-CPU backend, so the RMW falls "
"back to CPU serialisation and the publisher copies the frame back to host "
"memory before publishing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:155
msgid "Side-by-side comparison"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:157
msgid "$ ros2 launch robot_arm_demo robot_arm_compare.launch.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:161
msgid ""
"This starts both pipelines at once so you can compare their throughput "
"visually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:164
msgid ""
"All three launch files accept ``headless:=true`` to run without a display "
"window (useful for benchmarking on a headless box)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:168
